@* Without the corner X. Worth knowing what you are giving up: Escape and the backdrop still
   close it, because both are the dialog element's, not the button's — but a panel with no
   visible way out is one people learn to distrust. Leave it off only when the footer has one. *@
<SheetTrigger Target="sheet-no-close" Variant="outline">Open</SheetTrigger>

<Sheet Id="sheet-no-close" ShowCloseButton="false">
    <SheetHeader>
        <SheetTitle>Move to project</SheetTitle>
        <SheetDescription>No corner X — the footer carries the way out.</SheetDescription>
    </SheetHeader>
    <SheetFooter>
        <Button>Move</Button>
        <SheetClose>Cancel</SheetClose>
    </SheetFooter>
</Sheet>
